<description>
Pack the hollow square frames into a contiguous strip ordered by their original positions.

Input structure
- A black-background scene of separated monochrome 4x4 objects: hollow square frames and solid square distractors.
Rule
- Keep only the hollow frames and paste them edge-to-edge into one strip.
- If the hollow-frame positions spread more by column than row, pack left-to-right ordered by column; otherwise pack top-to-bottom ordered by row.
Key insight
- The solid blocks are distractors; the hollow frames are the retained sprites, and their dominant layout axis determines the output strip.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_in_order",
  "src": "hollow 4x4 foreground frame sprites s, ignoring solid 4x4 blocks",
  "dst": "contiguous output sprite slots d along the hollow-frame dominant axis",
  "match_cond": "rank(s by position on the chosen axis) == rank(d)",
  "transform": "crop each frame to its bbox and paste the crops edge-to-edge without recoloring",
  "multi_step": "choose horizontal packing when frame column span exceeds row span; choose vertical packing when row span exceeds column span",
  "grid_shape": "common 4x4 frame crop size multiplied by number of hollow frames along the chosen packing axis"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 18-24 rows x 16-22 cols, black (0) background
  objects:
    count: 4-6 total, each a distinct non-zero color on a 4x4 bounding box
    types:
      frame: hollow 4x4 square (border=color, interior=bg); count 2-3
      solid: filled 4x4 square (all cells=color); count 2-3
    color_8: always appears as one of the solids [observed]
    placement: non-overlapping, min gap >= 1 cell between any two objects
  axis_rule:
    row_span: max(frame_rows) - min(frame_rows)
    col_span: max(frame_cols) - min(frame_cols)
    constraint: row_span != col_span
    packing: horizontal if col_span > row_span, else vertical
    frame positions must have unique values on the packing axis (unique cols if horizontal, unique rows if vertical)
  output:
    shape: 4 x (4*N_frames) if horizontal, (4*N_frames) x 4 if vertical
    content: frames cropped and packed edge-to-edge, sorted by position on the dominant axis (left-to-right or top-to-bottom)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick N_frames in [2,3] and N_solids in [1,3]. Pick N_frames + N_solids distinct colors (1-9); always include color 8 assigned to a solid.
    2. Build output strip of N_frames hollow 4x4 frames packed edge-to-edge, each a different color.
    3. Choose packing axis (horizontal or vertical) randomly.
    4. Choose grid size (rows in [18,24], cols in [16,22]) large enough to fit all objects with gaps.
    5. Place each frame at a random position such that frames have distinct values on the packing axis, col_span > row_span (horizontal) or row_span > col_span (vertical), and no overlap with min 1-cell gap.
    6. Place N_solids solid 4x4 blocks (including color-8 one) at remaining positions with same gap constraints.
    7. Input is the composed grid; output is the strip from step 2.
